    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                The model for the growth of a population is given by
                <md>
                    y(t) = y_0e^{kt},
                </md>
                where <m>k</m> is the positive growth rate of the population.
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find the sensitivity function in the population size
                    dependent on changing the parameter <m>k</m>, i.e.,
                    <m>S(y,k)</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Interpret the meaning of your calculation in the context of
                    the scenario.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What conclusions can you make about how confident we can be
                    in the output of this model?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>
</worksheet>